   "text": {
    "L1": "Time uses groups of 60, not groups of 100.",
    "L2": "Sixty seconds make one minute, and sixty minutes make one hour.",
    "L3": "So two hours contain 120 minutes, because 2 times 60 is 120.",
    "L4": "A quarter of an hour is 15 minutes, half is 30, and three-quarters is 45.",
    "L5": "Now bust the myth: 1.5 hours is not 1 hour 50 minutes.",
    "L6": "The .5 means half an hour. Half an hour is 30 minutes, so 1.5 hours is 90 minutes.",
    "L7": "For the worked example, two and a quarter hours is 120 plus 15, or 135 minutes.",
    "L8": "Your turn: choose the conversion that follows the rule of 60."
   },
